@startuml 08-state-branch
!include _style.iuml
title Branch lifecycle (draft)

[*] --> Forked : fork(parent, SV)
Forked --> Active : first op
Active --> Active : ops
Active --> Paused : stop upstreaming
Paused --> Active : resume upstreaming
Active --> Proposed : ask for review
Proposed --> Active : changes requested
Proposed --> Merged : accept → replay into parent
Proposed --> Abandoned : reject
Active --> Abandoned : discard
Merged --> [*]
Abandoned --> [*]

Proposed : onion skin and redline\nrendered for reviewers
Merged : ops are kept,\nso the branch is still history
Abandoned : kept as history;\ncan be re-forked later

note right of Paused
  A paused queue is a local branch
  that isn't upstreaming. Its edits show
  as a translucent preview; releasing
  it is an ordinary merge.
end note
@enduml
